      {'id':'RPF-F016','severity':'medium','title':'Thimble flow accumulator is not absolute drift from the initial action','evidence':[evidence('code/rust/core_solvers/src/solver_quantum_lefschetz_thimble.rs',130,167)],'status':'bounded direct-source native probe reproduced','detail':'For S(z)=z²/2, correct gradient z, initial1+i and dt0.01, two steps give ImS0.99980001: true origin drift0.00019999 while stored drift is approximately1e-8. Keeping an absolute prior drift loses its sign. Store initial ImS or a signed cumulative difference and compare the actual origin delta.','limits':'Module explicitly proposal-only/archived metaphor. This is a failed diagnostic abort invariant, not evidence for a physical thimble.'},
